WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome back
and thank you for being here.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.000
Nice to see you. And --
-Nice to see you.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.767
-And thank you for doing the --
the TikTok dance challenge.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.701
Man, oh, man, that's a lot of
pressure.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:09.934
Do people dance --
-You did good.

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.701
-No, I didn't. But --
-I'm proud of you.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.767
-But when people are around you,
like, at a party or wedding,

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.300
are -- it's intimidating, right?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.534
Do people even dance,
or do they just leave the room?

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.501
-They do your moves.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:23.167
The one that's like --
-They're just sneaking out.

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.400
-Yeah. Sneaking out.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.167
-Congrats on "Te Felicito."

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.501
-Well said.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.334
Well pronounced.
Have a good accent.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.033
-It was good?
-"Te Felicito," perfect.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.601
-"Te Felicito."
Yeah, it came out,

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.367
and within a week,
it was the number one song,

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:38.400
so congrats on that.
-Thank you.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.367
-I mean, come on,
how do you do that?

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.667
That's got to feel good, right?

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:44.067
-Yeah, I mean, I'm -- Yeah.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:47.100
You know, I don't put out music
too often, because to me,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.501
it's a priority to dedicate time
to my kids.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.367
But when I do it, I focus.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.767
So -- yeah.
-Yeah, you do it right.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:58.133
-Yeah, I had to -- I had to
dedicate, like, three months

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.167
to just prepare the video.
And --

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.501
-I love the video, by the way.
-Yeah.

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.968
-Where did the concept
of the video come from?

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:07.601
-Actually, you know,
the creators of the video

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:08.934
are my kids.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.634
-They are?
-They came up with the idea.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.100
-No way.
-Can you believe?

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.501
-Yeah, they are pretty creative
kids.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.734
-Yeah.
-They just said, "Hey, what?"

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:17.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.734
-You know, I didn't have
any idea what to do.

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:22.501
-Yeah.
-When I'm about to produce

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.167
a video,
it's like a white canvas.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:28.234
And -- I have to kind of, like,
sit and think

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.334
about what I'm going to do.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.300
-And I had no idea
what I wanted to do.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.133
So I asked my kids to listen to
the song, close their eyes --

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:35.434
-Yes.
-And listen to the song.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:38.634
And my little one, Sasha,
came up with the robot idea.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:42.033
He said, "Mommy, I imagine you
dancing with a robot."

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.000
And -- And Milan came up with
the green fire.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.033
And I loved those two ideas.
And I took them to a director.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.434
And that was the whole --
the departure.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.300
-I want to show -- I want to
show a little --

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.067
Let me show the clip.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:56.300
Here's a clip of the music
video, "Te Felicito."

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.400
Check it out.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.167
-♪ Con tu papel continúa ♪

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:01.734
♪ Te queda bien ese show ♪

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:05.701
♪ Te felicito, qué bien actúas ♪

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.634
♪ De eso no me cabe duda ♪

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.267
♪ Con tu papel continúa ♪

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.734
♪ Te queda bien ese show ♪

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:15.934
♪ Te felicito, qué bien actúas ♪

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.467
-I mean, come on.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.000
Dancing with a robot?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.234
-Yeah, I think kids are
extremely creative, all of them.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.901
-Yeah, they are.
-And as adults, we just have to

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.167
take their ideas seriously.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.601
-Yeah, I -- do you think they're
going to grow up

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:29.167
and be in the music business
and be producers or musicians?

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:30.601
-I don't know.
I don't know.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:34.167
And I want them to do whatever
they feel passionate about.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:38.734
But I would like for them to
have music in their lives,

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:42.367
because music
gives them so much --

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.133
it's a good companion, you know?
In life.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.601
-It really is.
-And it's a good refuge.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:46.801
It's like -- [ Laughs ]
-Yeah.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:47.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.133
-And --
-It's always there for you.

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:52.267
-And they're learning piano,
they play the drums.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.601
-I heard when you were little,
you almost didn't get

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.601
into choir or something.
Is that true?

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.767
-That's true. Sadly. Yeah.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.934
-Who wouldn't have Shakira
in their choir?!

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:01.934
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:03.300
Really?
-My music teacher.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.801
-Wow.
-He didn't like my voice.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:07.534
He thought I was too disruptive
for the choir,

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.133
because my voice
was too strong.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:12.000
And, yeah, he never let me
in the choir,

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.601
and it was a huge frustration
for me.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.901
-Yeah.
-And even my classmates

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.434
teased me.
They used to tease me,

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:20.734
and they used to say that
I sounded like a goat.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:21.934
I hope it was a cute goat.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.000
Now -- now you are the G.O.A.T.,
so there you go.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.200
You did it.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:28.667
Showed them.
-Well, you know, my parents --

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.968
-A global music superstar.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.200
-Well, you know,
it was pretty hard

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.334
because it was some sort of --

00:03:35.334 --> 00:03:38.701
I think it was a way of
bullying, you know?

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.234
-Sure.
-Like, I felt bullied in a way.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:41.734
-Yeah.
-But --

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:44.467
-Did you almost think about not
going forward, not singing?

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:48.767
-Well, thanks to my parents,
I didn't, because my parents

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:54.067
actually reinforced and
reaffirmed my identity

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:58.067
as a singer. And they were --
they said -- especially my dad

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:02.567
always said that I didn't have
to change my vibrato.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:06.334
I had to protect that vibrato
and never ever change it,

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:10.300
because it was -- he always said
that a voice without vibrato

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.367
is not worth it.
It's not a voice, you know?

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:16.067
And so, I kept my vibrato,
and that's kind of my signature.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:17.234
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.701
-Thanks mom and dad.
-My goat signature.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.701
-Your goat signature, yeah.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:24.601
I know in New York, you were
recently at a Mets game

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:25.901
and cheering on the Mets.

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.367
And I was like, "Oh, yeah,
I wonder how you do cheer

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.100
at a game," because you get very
excited

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.567
when you're cheering for
your sons, for your boys.

00:04:32.567 --> 00:04:33.734
I've seen --
-I do.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.234
-I mean, I've seen video.
-I get carried away.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:36.734
-You are one of those people.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:37.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:38.834
-One of those moms.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.067
-Yeah, you're one --
-Annoying moms.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.234
-Yeah, you just like --
[screams] and you scream.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:44.334
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Can you -- I mean,

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:45.968
do people tell you to, like,
chill out?

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.501
-I embarrass my kids.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:51.767
Actually, yeah, during -- my
little one -- the both of them,

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:54.868
actually, practice taekwondo.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:58.968
And whenever they participate in
a tournament, taekwondo, they --

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:01.000
I scream like a crazy woman.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.467
And the dojo master, last time,
he gave me two warnings.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:08.467
The second -- and he said --
-You can't warn Shakira.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.634
No, no, no, no, no.
-Yeah, he almost kicked me out.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:11.868
-Oh, my gosh.
-Because I was like,

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.701
"Kick him in the head!
Kick him in the head!"

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:14.901
You know, I --

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.501
-No, she's not kidding.

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.834
In fact, we asked you if you
have any video of you.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:22.567
We have video of you cheering
your son on when Sasha won

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:24.334
first place in karate --
in taekwondo.

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.367
Look at this.

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.234
-[ Speaking in Spanish ]

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:30.567
[ Shakira screaming
and cheering ]

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:34.968
-Oh, my God, Sasha!
Oh, my God, Sasha!

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.968
[ Screaming ]

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:39.067
[ Cheering ]

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:42.934
-That's a loving mom
right there.

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:46.467
That is a good mom.
That is -- that's so funny.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.267
Oh, my gosh. You would have
thought that you won.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:50.133
Oh, my goodness.
That's great.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:53.534
Let's talk about your new NBC
series, "Dancing With Myself."

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:55.801
-Yes.
-What is the idea behind this --

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:58.200
this show?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.267
-To offer people from all walks
of life and all ages --

00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:05.334
A platform where they can
showcase their talents,

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.601
but also their passion
for dance.

00:06:07.601 --> 00:06:09.100
You know, they don't have to be
virtuosos,

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.968
they don't have to be
professionals.

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:14.934
Most of them aren't.
But --

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:17.334
-I like that you're not looking
at me, by the way.

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:19.334
-Exactly. They just have to
dance like you.

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:22.701
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-No, They're --

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.667
-Yeah.
-The idea with the show is --

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:31.434
is just to offer an opportunity
and access to people from --

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:33.968
yeah, from everywhere, and --
-To dance.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:37.701
-To dance and to show their
true passion for dance.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:41.200
You know, like, we had --
for example, we had doctors

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.968
on the show, we had
construction workers,

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:45.400
we had people in the military.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.467
We had dentists -- a lot of
dentists, actually.

00:06:47.467 --> 00:06:49.033
-Wow.
-For some strange reason.

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:51.467
-It was almost called
"Dancing Dentists" at first.

00:06:51.467 --> 00:06:53.934
They changed the title to
"Dancing With Myself."

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:57.367
I know our buddy, Nick Jonas,
is on with you, too.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.167
-Yeah.
-And -- yeah, he's a good --

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.567
-He's awesome.
-Yeah, he's the best.

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:02.634
And between the two of you,
I would never want to be

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:04.334
in a dance contest.

00:07:04.334 --> 00:07:05.868
I want to --
I want to show a clip.

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:07.334
Here's a look at
"Dancing With Myself."

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:08.567
Check this out.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:12.334
-Jeremy, can I ask you
what you do for a living?

00:07:12.334 --> 00:07:15.667
-Absolutely. So, I am
a plus size model in a --

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey!

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:20.901
-You might not be the most
technical dancer,

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:22.334
but I don't care.

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:24.901
Every time I see you dance --
I don't know, it's something

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:27.634
contagious, something infectious
about what you're doing.

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:31.434
And I just want to see more
of you.

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:32.767
Can you show me a model face?

00:07:32.767 --> 00:07:33.968
[ Audience oohs ]

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.367
-Work. Pose.

00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:38.701
Pose, pose.
-No, I smile. [ Laughs ]

00:07:38.701 --> 00:07:40.334
-You know, I don't have
a model face,

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:41.434
so I have a mirror face.

00:07:41.434 --> 00:07:42.968
I go --
-I've never noticed it.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.033
Not once.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:46.100
-Work, Queen. Work.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.033
-Do you have a mirror face?
-No.

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.167
-Come on, Nick.

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:54.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:55.934
-Hey, not the lip bite.

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:58.000
-Yeah, that's how you do it,
right there.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.067
Shakira, everybody!

00:08:00.067 --> 00:08:04.968
"Dancing With Myself" premieres
May 31st at 10:00 P.M. on NBC.

